  "question": {
    "text": "The exothermic formation of $\\mathrm{ClF}_3$ is represented by the equation:\n$$\n\\mathrm{Cl}_{2(g)}+3 \\mathrm{~F}_{2(g)} \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{ClF}_{3(g)} ; \\Delta \\mathrm{r} \\mathrm{H}=-329 \\mathrm{~kJ}\n$$\nWhich of the following will increase the quantity of $\\mathrm{ClF}_3$ in an equilibrium mixture of $\\mathrm{Cl}_2, \\mathrm{~F}_2$ and $\\mathrm{ClF}_3$ ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rARNQ",
      "text": "\nIncreasing the temperature\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ASmSA",
      "text": "\nRemoving $\\mathrm{Cl}_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iZmpS",
      "text": "\nIncreasing the volume of the container\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rKLAC",
      "text": "\nAdding $\\mathrm{F}_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{M}_3 \\mathrm{~V}_3=\\mathrm{M}_1 \\mathrm{~V}_2+\\mathrm{M}_2 \\mathrm{~V}_2$\n$\\mathrm{M}=\\frac{480(1.5)+520(1.2)}{1000}=1.344 \\mathrm{M}$",
    "image": null
  },
